      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>It's not just about forgetting a date or a route. It's the slow death of who I am. Every day I lose a little more of my personality, my memories, my independence. It's like I'm watching myself vanish in slow motion. I don't want to wait until I'm just a body in a bed that doesn't even know its own name. There's no dignity in that. There has to be a better way to handle this than just waiting to be erased.",
